{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run && ID=$(/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport json;s=json.load(open('\"'state.json'));print([a['id'] for a in s['direct_checks'] if a['id'].startswith('8a227417')][0])\\\") && cd draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - \\\"\"'$ID\" <<'\"'PY'\nimport json,sys\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"review\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Semantic review of the second scenario for C9-durable-recorder-uses-the-instance-row (artifact %s, executed as 9519d068…), which covers the case where the recovering replica's own row already holds an instance so no panic occurs. The item assesses requirement versus predicate, the two-row legality, the oracle and its dependence on the recorder's own layout, identity, and the bounded consequences.\\\",\n \\\"artifact_id\\\":sys.argv[1],\n \\\"review_items\\\":[{\n  \\\"aspect\\\":\\\"checker_correspondence\\\",\n  \\\"status\\\":\\\"no_issue_found\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\",\\\"S19-durable-record\\\"],\n  \\\"report_title\\\":\\\"自身行已占用时记录了他实例的元数据\\\",\n  \\\"report_answer\\\":\\\"当恢复者自身行在同一编号已存在另一实例（own_row_seq 858993459、ACCEPTED）时，阶段一为所有者实例写记录：写入的 seq 等于自身行的 seq 而非新实例的 seq 0（recorded_matches_new_instance=false、recorded_matches_own_row=true，状态为自身行的 ACCEPTED），即稳定存储收到的是另一实例的 ballot 上下文，且不会 panic。该结论限于启用记录的调用方（默认 durable=false），解码使用记录器自身布局这一限制也已注明。\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Requirement versus predicate: the claim is that the metadata recorded for a phase-1 write must belong to the instance being written, and the predicate asserts recorded_matches_new_instance == true; the retained run reports false with recorded_matches_own_row true, so the assertion is evaluated on the decoded values and the comparison points at the other instance. Entry and legality: the call is the phase-1 entry with the owner's coordinates, which is what the prepare resolution invokes when it restarts phase 1 for another replica's instance, and two rows holding an instance at the same number is the ordinary shape of per-replica rows rather than an invented state. Oracle and observation: the harness decodes the bytes with the layout the recorder itself writes (status at byte 4, seq at bytes 5 to 8) and compares the decoded seq against both candidate records, which is what makes the attribution possible; claim C2 shows that layout is not readable as its writes suggest, and that caveat is recorded as a limitation rather than hidden, since the comparison here only needs to identify which record's values were written. Identity: the prerequisite and result events share instance 1.0. Contrary evidence and limits: the shipped configuration passes durable=false, so the path is inert by default; only one instance number is exercised; and the check does not decode the deps region. No counterevidence was found that the duty holds in this scope.\\\",\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"the recorded bytes are decoded with the recorder's own write layout, which claim C2 shows is not the layout its field writes imply\\\",\n   \\\"the durable path is inert in the shipped configuration (durable=false)\\\",\n   \\\"one instance number and one occupied own row are exercised; the deps region is not decoded\\\"]}]}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-review-c9b.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint(sub['artifact_id'])\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-review-c9b.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
