{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission-review-c9b.json\", \"summary\": \"Turn 55 reviewed the silent half of the durability call-site defect, completing that finding's two scenarios.\\n\\nState on entry. The first C9 artifact is confirmed (the absent own row panics while the instance lands under the owner's row). The second artifact, 8a2274171b4d486cba6de949531ef930 (executed as 9519d068…), reported violated with the oracle correspondence unreviewed, and its retained stream shows the case where the own row is occupied: recorded seq 858993459 equal to the own row's seq and not the new instance's seq 0, with the own row's ACCEPTED status.\\n\\nReview judgement (checker_correspondence, no_issue_found). Requirement versus predicate: the claim is that metadata recorded for a phase-1 write must belong to the instance being written, and the predicate asserts recorded_matches_new_instance == true; the run reports false with recorded_matches_own_row true, so the assertion is evaluated on decoded values and the comparison points at the other instance. Entry and legality: the call is the phase-1 entry with the owner's coordinates, which is what the prepare resolution invokes when it restarts phase 1 for another replica's instance, and two rows holding an instance at the same number is the ordinary shape of per-replica rows rather than an invented state. Oracle and observation: the harness decodes the bytes with the layout the recorder itself writes (status at byte 4, sequence at bytes 5-8) and compares the decoded value against both candidate records, which is what makes attribution possible; claim C2 shows that layout is not readable as its writes suggest, and that caveat is recorded as a limitation rather than hidden, since the comparison only needs to identify which record's values were written. Identity: the prerequisite and result events share instance 1.0. Limits: the shipped configuration passes durable=false, so the path is inert by default; one instance number and one occupied own row are exercised; and the deps region is not decoded. No counterevidence was found that the duty holds in this scope.\\n\\nEffect. C9 now stands as a two-scenario obligation — a crash on an absent record and a silent wrong-metadata write when the slot exists — both confirmed, and it remains distinct from C2, which concerns the layout of whatever the recorder writes. Audit spec version 12; the eight other settled claims (C1/C6/C7/C9 confirmed violations, C2/C3/C4 confirmed, C5/C8 bounded protections) and the two paused candidates are untouched, with only the scope-issue bookkeeping on the superseded C1 artifact still visible. No requirement, premise or earlier observation was weakened.\"}"}}
